The T1e prototype patch (DR-013 addendum), against the T1d net-next
base (net/core/dev.c). Applied when T1d's runs are done; the build
and the unpinned arm (n=8) follow the frozen rule in specs/p1-T1E.md.

--- a/net/core/dev.c
+++ b/net/core/dev.c
@@ -1630,17 +1630,39 @@ static int napi_threaded_poll(void *data);
 static int napi_kthread_create(struct napi_struct *n)
 {
 	int err = 0;
+	const struct cpumask *aff, *llc;
 
 	/* Create and wake up the kthread once to put it in
 	 * TASK_INTERRUPTIBLE mode to avoid the blocked task
 	 * warning and avoid work with loadavg.
 	 */
 	n->thread = kthread_run(napi_threaded_poll, n, "napi/%s-%d",
 				n->dev->name, n->napi_id);
 	if (IS_ERR(n->thread)) {
 		err = PTR_ERR(n->thread);
 		pr_err("kthread_run failed with err %d\n", err);
 		n->thread = NULL;
+	} else if (n->irq > 0) {
+		/* Default the threaded poller's cpumask to the L3
+		 * siblings of its vector's effective affinity. A floating
+		 * poller lands on remote L3/NUMA cpus and stalls under
+		 * sustained flood (the measured placement asymmetry).
+		 * The default is (re)applied on every thread (re)creation
+		 * because a driver reset destroys the thread -- the
+		 * threaded-NAPI lifecycle gap under discussion upstream
+		 * (June 2026 RFC). Only the single-cpu effective-affinity
+		 * case (per-channel MSI-X vectors) gets the default; the
+		 * spread case is left floating. A later userspace
+		 * set-affinity wins as usual.
+		 */
+		aff = irq_get_effective_affinity(n->irq);
+		if (aff && cpumask_weight(aff) == 1) {
+			llc = topology_llc_cpumask(cpumask_first(aff));
+			set_cpus_allowed_ptr(n->thread, llc);
+		}
 	}
 
 	return err;
 }

Semantics notes (facts for the report):
- The creation site is the single choke point: driver resets destroy
  and recreate the thread (the NAPI lifecycle), so a default set here
  is re-applied after every reset.
- irq_get_effective_affinity(n->irq) is read at creation time; mlx5
  narrows each comp vector's affinity to its channel cpu at irq
  creation, before the channel's napi threads are created.
- The patch does not touch napi_config; it composes with the merged
  napi_config affinity work (which covers IRQ affinity, not the
  thread).